<h3 id="updates">Registration and Updates</h3>
<p>
	After you activate VetPress, WordPress opens <strong>Appearance &gt; Theme Registration</strong>. Register with the license key from your <a href="https://www.proteusthemes.com/account/" target="_blank">ProteusThemes account</a>, or with the purchase code from your ThemeForest download, as the registration page explains.
</p>
<p>
	Register before you use <strong>One Click Demo Import</strong>: the import stays locked until you do. Registration also lets the <strong>ProteusThemes Support</strong> plugin send us your <a href="#support">site report</a>.
</p>
<p>
	<strong>Automatic updates:</strong> once you're registered, new VetPress versions show in <strong>Dashboard &gt; Updates</strong> and install from there. For a ThemeForest purchase, also create and save the <strong>Envato token</strong> the registration page asks for. It is separate from your purchase code.
</p>
<p>
	If an update you expect isn't showing, open <strong>Dashboard &gt; Updates</strong> and click <strong>Check Again</strong>. Your content and your Site Editor changes are kept when you update.
</p>
<h4 id="manual-updates">Updating manually</h4>
<p>
	You can also install a new version yourself, for example when an update from the dashboard fails.
</p>
<p>
	<strong>Before you update:</strong>
</p>
<ul>
	<li>Back up your site's files and database.</li>
	<li>Check that your server still meets the <a href="#installation">requirements</a>.</li>
	<li>Your pages, posts, menus, styles and Site Editor changes are stored in the database, so they are kept. Changes made directly to the theme's files are overwritten. Changes in a child theme are kept.</li>
</ul>
<p>
	<strong>Download the latest version.</strong> If you bought the theme on ThemeForest, open your <a href="https://themeforest.net/downloads" target="_blank">ThemeForest downloads</a>, click <strong>Download</strong> next to the theme and choose <strong>Installable WordPress file only</strong>. The "All files &amp; documentation" package can't be installed as it is. If you bought it in our shop, download it from your <a href="https://www.proteusthemes.com/account/" target="_blank">ProteusThemes account</a>.
</p>
<p>
	<strong>Updating with Upload Theme:</strong>
</p>
<ol>
	<li>Go to <strong>Appearance &gt; Themes &gt; Add Theme &gt; Upload Theme</strong>, choose the zip and click <strong>Install Now</strong>.</li>
	<li>WordPress shows the installed and uploaded versions side by side. Click <strong>Replace installed with uploaded</strong>.</li>
	<li>If the theme asks you to install or update plugins, follow its notice.</li>
</ol>
<p>
	<strong>Updating with FTP or your host's file manager:</strong>
</p>
<ol>
	<li>Unzip the theme zip on your computer. Inside is the theme folder, the one with <code>style.css</code> in it.</li>
	<li>On your server, open <code>wp-content/themes/</code> and download a copy of the current theme folder as a backup.</li>
	<li>Upload the new theme folder into <code>wp-content/themes/</code>, replacing the existing files. Many host file managers let you upload the zip, extract it there and overwrite all files.</li>
</ol>
<div class="info">
	A template or template part you changed in the Site Editor keeps your version after an update, so it doesn't pick up the theme's changes to it. To switch one back to the theme's latest version, open it in <strong>Appearance &gt; Editor</strong>, open the <strong>⋮</strong> menu and choose <strong>Reset</strong>. That removes your changes to it.
</div>
